 {"startPos": 1997,
  "moduleName": "Init.Prelude",
  "kind": "definition",
  "fullName": "rfl",
  "endPos": 2000,
  "detail":
  "```lean\nrfl.{u} {α : Sort u} {a : α} : a = a\n```\n***\n`rfl : a = a` is the unique constructor of the equality type. This is the\nsame as `Eq.refl` except that it takes `a` implicitly instead of explicitly.\n\nThis is a more powerful theorem than it may appear at first, because although\nthe statement of the theorem is `a = a`, Lean will allow anything that is\ndefinitionally equal to that type. So, for instance, `2 + 2 = 4` is proven in\nLean by `rfl`, because both sides are the same up to definitional equality.\n\n***\n*import Init.Prelude*",
  "definitionStartPos": {"line": 294, "column": 21},
  "definitionPath":
  "/Users/hattoriseiji/.elan/toolchains/leanprover--lean4---v4.10.0-rc2/src/lean/Init/Prelude.lean",
  "definitionEndPos": {"line": 294, "column": 24}},
